<template>
    <heading>Command State Machine</heading>
    <keywords><li>startup</li><li>state machine</li><li>project selection</li></keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p><code>startState</code> is the initial state. It calls <code>SelectCreateProject</code> for a <code>ModalDialog</code> command naming that dialog, and calls <code>ReloadProject</code> for a <code>ReloadProject</code> command. <code>SelectCreateProject</code> displays the modal in its entry code. When it receives <code>SelectProject</code>, it calls the <code>SelectProject</code> child state. The parent state is suspended during the call, so it keeps the modal open while the child performs selection and loading. If the child returns <code>ProjectLoaded</code>, the parent closes the modal and returns. If it returns <code>ProjectPickerAborted</code>, the parent stays active and the modal remains open for another attempt.</p>
        <p><code>EditArticle</code> opens the selected article in a dialog and waits for <code>CancelEditArticle</code> or <code>SaveArticle</code>. Saving runs in a child state; on success the model reload notification refreshes the panes and the edit operation closes the dialog. A validation or storage failure returns to the editor with its draft and error message intact.</p>
        <p>The <code>SelectProject</code> child starts <a href="#28.lp5"><code>asyncSelectProject(event)</code></a> in its entry code, during dispatch of the initiating command. This matters because local selection invokes the browser's <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Window/showDirectoryPicker">directory picker</a>, which requires <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/Security/Defenses/User_activation">transient user activation</a> from the click. While the child is waiting, it handles <code>ProjectLoaded</code> and <code>ProjectPickerAborted</code>; another <code>SelectProject</code> command does not match either handler, so it cannot start a second load. The async function dispatches the <a href="#20.lp5"><code>ProjectLoaded</code> controller command</a> after loading. Separately, the model emits a <code>ProjectLoaded</code> event that refreshes the view. Project creation is not implemented. This machine uses the controller's supported calls and returns.</p>
        <p>The <code>ReloadProject</code> child starts <code>asyncReloadProject()</code> in its entry code and returns when it receives the <code>ProjectLoaded</code> controller command. Loading also emits the model's <code>ProjectLoaded</code> event, which lets the view refresh. Both child operations use calls and returns, which the controller supports.</p>
        <p>Indentation guide: <code>state</code> starts in column 1, <code>on</code> in column 4, and <code>-&gt;()</code> in column 2. These positions keep the directive structure visually aligned. Indent each directive's JavaScript right-hand side at the current code level, starting in column 7 and adding four columns for each nested JavaScript block. Keep directive tokens in their fixed columns even inside a JavaScript condition. Ordinary JavaScript uses the same indentation as a directive's right-hand side. Indentation has no effect on how directives are parsed.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>Command state machine</name>
        <code><![CDATA[
const stateMachineSource = `
state startState
   on EditArticle
 ->() EditArticle

   on ModalDialog
      if (event.dialogName === "SelectCreateProject") {
 ->()     SelectCreateProject
      }

   on ReloadProject
 ->() ReloadProject

state SelectCreateProject
      view.showModalDialog("SelectCreateProject");

   on SelectProject
 ->() SelectProject
      if (event.name === "ProjectLoaded") {
          view.closeModalDialog("SelectCreateProject");
          return;
      }

state EditArticle
      view.showArticleEditor(event.filename);

   on SaveArticle
 ->() SaveArticle
      if (event.name === "ArticleSaved") {
          view.closeModalDialog("EditArticle");
          return;
      }
      if (event.name === "ArticleSaveFailed") {
          view.showArticleEditorError(event.message);
      }

   on CancelEditArticle
      view.closeModalDialog("EditArticle");
      return;

state SaveArticle
      asyncSaveArticle(event);

   on ArticleSaved
      return;

   on ArticleSaveFailed
      return;

state SelectProject
      asyncSelectProject(event);

   on ProjectLoaded
      return;

   on ProjectPickerAborted
      return;

state ReloadProject
      asyncReloadProject();

   on ProjectLoaded
      return;
`;
]]></code></section></template>
